    {
      "title": "Values & data types",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "value",
          "target": "Wert",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-value"
        },
        {
          "en": "number",
          "target": "Zahl",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-number"
        },
        {
          "en": "integer",
          "target": "Ganzzahl",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The type keyword `int` in code stays English.",
          "anchor": "term-integer"
        },
        {
          "en": "float / decimal",
          "target": "Gleitkommazahl",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "\"Dezimalzahl\" is an acceptable plain-language gloss when precision doesn't matter.",
          "anchor": "term-float-decimal"
        },
        {
          "en": "character",
          "target": "Zeichen",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-character"
        },
        {
          "en": "true / false",
          "target": "wahr / falsch",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Not capitalized in prose.",
          "anchor": "term-true-false"
        },
        {
          "en": "array",
          "target": "Array",
          "use": "en",
          "notes": "Dominant in modern German teaching material over the older, theory-flavored \"Feld\". No gloss needed, \"Array\" is standard vocabulary now.",
          "anchor": "term-array"
        },
        {
          "en": "dictionary",
          "target": "Wörterbuch",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "General prose term. Python-specific material may say \"Dictionary\"/\"dict\" instead; do not mix within one document.",
          "anchor": "term-dictionary"
        },
        {
          "en": "element",
          "target": "Element",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Fully naturalized.",
          "anchor": "term-element"
        },
        {
          "en": "index",
          "target": "Index",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Learned plural: \"Indizes\".",
          "anchor": "term-index"
        },
        {
          "en": "string",
          "target": "String",
          "use": "en",
          "notes": "Where the source `<define>`s it, gloss as \"String (Zeichenkette)\", then use \"String\" throughout. Exception: in the string concept itself, lean more on \"Zeichenkette\" if it aids teaching.",
          "anchor": "term-string"
        },
        {
          "en": "Boolean",
          "target": "boolescher Wert",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Standard textbook/prose form. The type keyword `bool`/`Boolean` in code stays English.",
          "anchor": "term-boolean"
        },
        {
          "en": "data type",
          "target": "Datentyp",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-data-type"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Functions & control flow",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "if statement",
          "target": "if-Anweisung",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The `if` keyword stays English in code and in this compound; \"Anweisung\" is translated.",
          "anchor": "term-if-statement"
        },
        {
          "en": "condition",
          "target": "Bedingung",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Ordinary word; stands alone.",
          "anchor": "term-condition"
        },
        {
          "en": "comparison",
          "target": "Vergleich",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Ordinary word; stands alone.",
          "anchor": "term-comparison"
        },
        {
          "en": "expression",
          "target": "Ausdruck",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Distinct from \"Anweisung\" (statement).",
          "anchor": "term-expression"
        },
        {
          "en": "operator",
          "target": "Operator",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-operator"
        },
        {
          "en": "statement (executable)",
          "target": "Anweisung",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The imperative sense: a line of code that does something and gets executed.",
          "anchor": "term-statement"
        },
        {
          "en": "statement (logical claim)",
          "target": "Aussage",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The proposition sense: a claim that is true or false. Keep distinct from \"Anweisung\".",
          "anchor": "term-statement-2"
        },
        {
          "en": "function",
          "target": "Funktion",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The *keyword* `function` in code stays English; the concept in prose is \"Funktion\".",
          "anchor": "term-function"
        },
        {
          "en": "to call (a function)",
          "target": "aufrufen",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Separable verb: \"ruft die Funktion auf\".",
          "anchor": "term-to-call"
        },
        {
          "en": "to define (a function)",
          "target": "definieren",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-to-define"
        },
        {
          "en": "parameter",
          "target": "Parameter",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Declaration-site name. Masculine, unchanged plural: \"der Parameter, die Parameter\".",
          "anchor": "term-parameter"
        },
        {
          "en": "argument",
          "target": "Argument",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Call-site value. Neuter, distinct gender from \"Parameter\": \"das Argument, die Argumente\".",
          "anchor": "term-argument"
        },
        {
          "en": "input (to a function)",
          "target": "Eingabewert",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Distinct from general \"Eingabe\" (user input).",
          "anchor": "term-input"
        },
        {
          "en": "output",
          "target": "Ausgabe",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The function's result specifically is \"Rückgabewert\"; \"Ausgabe\" is the general/printed sense.",
          "anchor": "term-output"
        },
        {
          "en": "to return (a value)",
          "target": "zurückgeben",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Separable verb: \"gibt den Wert zurück\".",
          "anchor": "term-to-return"
        },
        {
          "en": "return value",
          "target": "Rückgabewert",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Keep distinct from the verb above.",
          "anchor": "term-return-value"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Loops, state & program flow",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "keyword",
          "target": "Schlüsselwort",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-keyword"
        },
        {
          "en": "variable",
          "target": "Variable",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Feminine noun: \"die Variable, die Variablen\".",
          "anchor": "term-variable"
        },
        {
          "en": "assignment",
          "target": "Zuweisung",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The noun.",
          "anchor": "term-assignment"
        },
        {
          "en": "to assign",
          "target": "zuweisen",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Takes a dative object: \"Der Wert wird der Variablen zugewiesen.\"",
          "anchor": "term-to-assign"
        },
        {
          "en": "code block",
          "target": "Block",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Keep distinct from \"scope\" (Gültigkeitsbereich) below; do not conflate.",
          "anchor": "term-code-block"
        },
        {
          "en": "error",
          "target": "Fehler",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-error"
        },
        {
          "en": "nested",
          "target": "verschachtelt",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "e.g. \"verschachtelte Schleife\" = nested loop.",
          "anchor": "term-nested"
        },
        {
          "en": "iteration",
          "target": "Iteration",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "\"Durchlauf\" is a friendlier beginner gloss for a single pass through a loop.",
          "anchor": "term-iteration"
        },
        {
          "en": "to run / execute (code)",
          "target": "ausführen",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Separable verb: \"führt das Programm aus\".",
          "anchor": "term-to-run-execute"
        },
        {
          "en": "loop",
          "target": "Schleife",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "English \"loop\" is never used in prose.",
          "anchor": "term-loop"
        },
        {
          "en": "for loop",
          "target": "for-Schleife",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Keep the `for` keyword in code font; translate only \"Schleife\".",
          "anchor": "term-for-loop"
        },
        {
          "en": "while loop",
          "target": "while-Schleife",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "As above, with `while`.",
          "anchor": "term-while-loop"
        },
        {
          "en": "loop body",
          "target": "Schleifenrumpf",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "\"Schleifenkörper\" is an equally valid alternative; pick one and stay consistent within a document.",
          "anchor": "term-loop-body"
        },
        {
          "en": "increment",
          "target": "erhöhen",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The verb. Reads more naturally for beginners than the loanword \"inkrementieren\".",
          "anchor": "term-increment"
        },
        {
          "en": "scope",
          "target": "Gültigkeitsbereich",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Keep distinct from \"Block\" (code block) above.",
          "anchor": "term-scope"
        },
        {
          "en": "class",
          "target": "Klasse",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-class"
        },
        {
          "en": "method",
          "target": "Methode",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-method"
        },
        {
          "en": "property",
          "target": "Eigenschaft",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "More intuitive for beginners than the formal OOP term \"Attribut\".",
          "anchor": "term-property"
        },
        {
          "en": "object",
          "target": "Objekt",
          "use": "de",
          "anchor": "term-object"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tooling & engineering",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "workflow",
          "target": "Workflow",
          "use": "en",
          "notes": "Duden-recognized loanword; distinct from the curriculum sense.",
          "anchor": "term-workflow"
        },
        {
          "en": "deploy",
          "target": "ausrollen",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "The verb, more natural for beginners than the loanword \"deployen\". Noun form: \"Deployment\".",
          "anchor": "term-deploy"
        },
        {
          "en": "tool / tooling",
          "target": "Tool",
          "use": "en",
          "notes": "Shorter and what developers actually say; \"Werkzeug\" is a legitimate native alternative but not the default here.",
          "anchor": "term-tool-tooling"
        },
        {
          "en": "module",
          "target": "Modul",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Fully naturalized.",
          "anchor": "term-module"
        },
        {
          "en": "algorithm",
          "target": "Algorithmus",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Irregular Latin plural: \"die Algorithmen\".",
          "anchor": "term-algorithm"
        },
        {
          "en": "edge case",
          "target": "Randfall",
          "use": "de",
          "notes": "Where the source `<define>`s it, gloss as \"Randfall (Edge Case)\". Keep distinct from \"Grenzfall\" (a boundary value) and \"Sonderfall\" (a special/exceptional case), which are not synonyms.",
          "anchor": "term-edge-case"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
